Requires `CLERK_SECRET_KEY` + `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` (injected in Cloud Agent env).

## MCP Playwright (interactive)

When debugging a specific click flow, use the **Playwright MCP** tools (`browser_navigate`,
`browser_click`, `browser_snapshot`, `browser_take_screenshot`) after minting cookies via the
auth helpers above — or run the committed scripts first.

## What HTTP-only audit still covers

`fetchAuditJson` + served HTML probes remain valid for **API/data** audits. UI validation is
**additive**, not either/or — run both when validating a desk change.

## On failure

If Playwright fails, diagnose (chunk load, auth cookie, deploy mid-rollout) and retry — do not
fall back to claiming UI validation is unavailable.

## Post-deploy delivery (standing — do NOT ask the operator)

After **any** UI-facing merge to `main` (especially Night Hawk / Vector / Legacy boards):

1. **Monitor** `ECR push (production)` on `main` until `completed` (poll `gh run list --workflow ecr-push-production.yml`).
2. **Verify live** on `https://blackouttrades.com` with Playwright + Clerk admin auth — do not stop at merge.
3. **Screenshot** the changed surface (click rows, open rails, exercise the fix) → `/opt/cursor/artifacts/`.
4. **Deliver** screenshots + deploy verdict in the same thread — **never ask** "want me to monitor?" or "should I screenshot?".

Night Hawk boards: `node scripts/audit/nighthawk-boards-prod-screenshots.mjs` (Vector + Legacy);
Legacy detail rail must show `Why we picked it` / `What to watch` on row select without extra tab clicks.
